      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "An image demonstrating point filtering vs. bilinear vs. bicubic interpolation. Note how the \"hotspots\" shift off pixel centers. This is part of what makes bicubic so powerful for low-res textures, it effectively \"subdivides\" a texture, smoothing out peaks and valleys, so everything just looks smooth and beautiful. Pixilation goes away, and round details stay round.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
